  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 7,
    "summary": "David trusts in the Lord, who will judge the people—God is angry with the wicked.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "O Lord my God, in thee do I put my trust: save me from all them that persecute me, and deliver me:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 7:1",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Lest he tear my soul like a lion, rending it in pieces, while there is none to deliver.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 44
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 70
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 7:2",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "O Lord my God, if I have done this; if there be iniquity in my hands;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 7:3",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "If I have rewarded evil unto him that was at peace with me; (yea, I have delivered him that without cause is mine enemy:)",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 7:4",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Let the enemy persecute my soul, and take it; yea, let him tread down my life upon the earth, and lay mine honour in the dust. Selah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 7:5",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Arise, O Lord, in thine anger, lift up thyself because of the rage of mine enemies: and awake for me to the judgment that thou hast commanded.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 103
          },
          {
            "start": 117,
            "end": 121
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 7:6",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "So shall the congregation of the people compass thee about: for their sakes therefore return thou on high.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 7:7",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "The Lord shall judge the people: judge me, O Lord, according to my righteousness, and according to mine integrity that is in me.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "TG Jesus Christ, Judge."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 114,
            "end": 121
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Jesus Christ, Judge.",
            "prettyString": "TG Jesus Christ, Judge",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Jesus Christ, Judge",
                "entryId": "tg-jesus-christ-judge",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 7:8",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Oh let the wickedness of the wicked come to an end; but establish the just: for the righteous God trieth the hearts and reins.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 104,
            "text": "TG Test."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Test.",
            "prettyString": "TG Test",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Test",
                "entryId": "tg-test",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 7:9",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "My defence is of God, which saveth the upright in heart.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 13
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 7:10",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "God judgeth the righteous, and God is angry with the wicked every day.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 43,
            "text": "TG God, Indignation of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG God, Indignation of.",
            "prettyString": "TG God, Indignation of",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "God, Indignation of",
                "entryId": "tg-god-indignation-of",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 7:11",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "If he turn not, he will whet his sword; he hath bent his bow, and made it ready.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 7:12",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "He hath also prepared for him the instruments of death; he ordaineth his arrows against the persecutors.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Psalms 7:13",
        "book": "Psalms",
        "chapter": 7,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
